{"authored" [{"question" "q-164380" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The projection of the intersection between the hyperboloid of two sheets $-\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{18}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}+(z-2)^{2}=-1$ and the plane $z=3$ onto the $xy$-plane is a hyperbola. What are the lengths of the semi-axes of the hyperbola?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14035554/state.json" "file_sha256" "def1579efa9e17ed2eeb15ff956d4dffcaf647b3ec61664fe665a85b779303bf" "basis" 1238 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14035554/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-164380" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the intersection of the hyperboloid and the plane $z=3,$ we substitute $z=3$ into the equation of the hyperboloid:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{18}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}+(3-2)^{2} & =-1 \\\\ -\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{18}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}+1 & =-1 \\\\ -\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{18}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2} & =-2 \\\\ \\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{18}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2} & =2 \\\\ \\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{36}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{{6}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{2}^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of a hyperbola with semi-axes of lengths $6$ and $2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14035554/state.json" "file_sha256" "def1579efa9e17ed2eeb15ff956d4dffcaf647b3ec61664fe665a85b779303bf" "basis" 1238 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14035554/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-164380" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14035554/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b65df1969efc25f29516062e2caa1a3c57e4f6191012bead8afceea49150b42e" "basis" 1238 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14035554/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-164380" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14035554/state.json" "file_sha256" "def1579efa9e17ed2eeb15ff956d4dffcaf647b3ec61664fe665a85b779303bf" "basis" 1238 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14035554/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-164380" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "$18$ and $2$"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14035554/state.json" "file_sha256" "def1579efa9e17ed2eeb15ff956d4dffcaf647b3ec61664fe665a85b779303bf" "basis" 1238 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14035554/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-164380" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "$3\\sqrt{2}$ and $\\sqrt{2}$"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14035554/state.json" "file_sha256" "def1579efa9e17ed2eeb15ff956d4dffcaf647b3ec61664fe665a85b779303bf" "basis" 1238 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14035554/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-164380" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "$6$ and $2$"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14035554/state.json" "file_sha256" "def1579efa9e17ed2eeb15ff956d4dffcaf647b3ec61664fe665a85b779303bf" "basis" 1238 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14035554/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-164380" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "$9$ and $4$"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14035554/state.json" "file_sha256" "def1579efa9e17ed2eeb15ff956d4dffcaf647b3ec61664fe665a85b779303bf" "basis" 1238 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14035554/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-164380" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "$\\sqrt{6}$ and $\\sqrt{3}$"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14035554/state.json" "file_sha256" "def1579efa9e17ed2eeb15ff956d4dffcaf647b3ec61664fe665a85b779303bf" "basis" 1238 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14035554/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-164380" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$6$ and $2$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14035554/state.json" "file_sha256" "def1579efa9e17ed2eeb15ff956d4dffcaf647b3ec61664fe665a85b779303bf" "basis" 1238 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14035554/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-164278" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the hyperboloid of two sheets $\\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{5}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4}=-1,$ find its $x$-intercepts." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-164278" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the $x$-intercepts, we plug $y=0$ and $z=0$ into the equation: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{5}+\\frac{{0}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{0}^{2}}{4} & =-1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{5} & =-1 \\\\ (x+4)^{2} & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation has no (real) solutions.\n\nTherefore, the hyperboloid does not intersect the $x$-axis." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-164278" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bf97a5acc6acd2fe54bfdd2de22861374226df9798b45f6cf8422eff6e03593a"} {"question" "q-164278" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-164278" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$(-4+\\sqrt{5},0,0)$ only"] ["text" "$(-4,0,0)$  only"] ["text" "$(-4,0,0)$ and $(4,0,0)$"] ["text" "$(-4-\\sqrt{5},0,0)$ and $(-4+\\sqrt{5},0,0)$"] ["text" "The hyperboloid does not intersect the $x$-axis"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-164278" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "The hyperboloid does not intersect the $x$-axis"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-35489" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the hyperboloid of one sheet $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{(z-2)^{2}}{16}=1$, find its $y$-intercepts." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-35489" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the $y$-intercepts, we plug $x=0$ and $z=0$ into the equation: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{0}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{(0-2)^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{1}{4} & =1 \\\\ (y-1)^{2}-1 & =4 \\\\ (y-1)^{2} & =5 \\\\ y-1 & =\\pm \\sqrt{5} \\\\ y & =1\\pm \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $y=1-\\sqrt{5}$ and $1+\\sqrt{5}.$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $y$-axis are $(0,1-\\sqrt{5},0)$ and $(0,1+\\sqrt{5},0).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-35489" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bf97a5acc6acd2fe54bfdd2de22861374226df9798b45f6cf8422eff6e03593a"} {"question" "q-35489" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-35489" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$(0,-4,0)$ and $(0,6,0)$"] ["text" "$(0,-\\sqrt{5},0)$ and $(0,\\sqrt{5},0)$"] ["text" "$(0,1-\\sqrt{5},0)$ and $(0,1+\\sqrt{5},0)$"] ["text" "$(0,4,0)$ and $(0,6,0)$"] ["text" "$(0,\\sqrt{5}-1,0)$ and $(0,\\sqrt{5}+1,0)$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-35489" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$(0,1-\\sqrt{5},0)$ and $(0,1+\\sqrt{5},0)$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-164272" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the hyperboloid of two sheets ${x}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(z+1)^{2}}{4}=-1,$ find its $z$-intercepts." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-164272" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the $z$-intercepts, we plug $x=0$ and $y=0$ into the equation: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{0}^{2}+\\frac{{0}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(z+1)^{2}}{4} & =-1 \\\\ -\\frac{(z+1)^{2}}{4} & =-1 \\\\ (z+1)^{2} & =4 \\\\ z+1 & =\\pm 2 \\\\ z & =-1\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $z=-3$ and $z=1.$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $z$-axis are $(0,0,-3)$ and $(0,0,1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-164272" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bf97a5acc6acd2fe54bfdd2de22861374226df9798b45f6cf8422eff6e03593a"} {"question" "q-164272" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-164272" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$(0,0,-1)$ only"] ["text" "$(0,0,-2)$ and $(0,0,2)$"] ["text" "$(0,0,-3)$ and $(0,0,1)$"] ["text" "$(0,0,-3)$ only"] ["text" "The hyperboloid does not intersect the $z$-axis"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-164272" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$(0,0,-3)$ and $(0,0,1)$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-164284" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the hyperboloid of two sheets $\\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{3}+\\frac{(y+6)^{2}}{5}-(z-1)^{2}=-1,$ find its $y$-intercepts." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-164284" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the $y$-intercepts, we plug $x=0$ and $z=0$ into the equation: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(0+3)^{2}}{3}+\\frac{(y+6)^{2}}{5}-(0-1)^{2} & =-1 \\\\ 3+\\frac{(y+6)^{2}}{5}-1 & =-1 \\\\ \\frac{(y+6)^{2}}{5} & =-3 \\\\ (y+6)^{2} & =-15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation has no (real) solutions.\n\nTherefore, the hyperboloid does not intersect the $y$-axis." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-164284" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bf97a5acc6acd2fe54bfdd2de22861374226df9798b45f6cf8422eff6e03593a"} {"question" "q-164284" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-1