"field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bf97a5acc6acd2fe54bfdd2de22861374226df9798b45f6cf8422eff6e03593a"} {"question" "q-164277" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-164277" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$(0,-2,0)$ and $(0,2,0)$"] ["text" "$(0,2,0)$ only"] ["text" "$(0,3-\\sqrt{2},0)$ and $(0,3+\\sqrt{2},0)$"] ["text" "$(0,3-\\sqrt{2},0)$ only"] ["text" "The hyperboloid does not intersect the $y$-axis"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-164277" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$(0,-2,0)$ and $(0,2,0)$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-164307" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the hyperboloid of one sheet $(x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}-(z-3)^{2}=1,$ find the domain of $z=z(x,y).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-164307" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the hyperboloid equation, we make $z$ the subject as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}-(z-3)^{2} & =1 \\\\ (x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}-1 & =(z-3)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(z-3)^{2} & =(x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}-1 \\\\ z-3 & =\\pm \\sqrt{(x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}-1} \\\\ z & =3\\pm \\sqrt{(x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the square root is defined only for non-negative arguments, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}-1 & \\ge 0 \\\\ (x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2} & \\ge 1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives the exterior of the circle $(x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}=1,$ which includes the boundary.\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ge 1}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-164307" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bf97a5acc6acd2fe54bfdd2de22861374226df9798b45f6cf8422eff6e03593a"} {"question" "q-164307" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-164307" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}<3}"] ["math" "{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}>1}"] ["math" "{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ge 1}"] ["math" "{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 3}"] ["math" "{R}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-164307" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ge 1}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-74015" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the hyperboloid of one sheet $\\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{7}+\\frac{(y+8)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(z-1)^{2}}{4}=1$, find the domain of $z=z(x,y).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-74015" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the hyperboloid equation, we make $z$ the subject as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{7}+\\frac{(y+8)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(z-1)^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{7}+\\frac{(y+8)^{2}}{2}-1 & =\\frac{(z-1)^{2}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(z-1)^{2} & =4(\\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{7}+\\frac{(y+8)^{2}}{2}-1) \\\\ z-1 & =\\pm 2\\sqrt{\\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{7}+\\frac{(y+8)^{2}}{2}-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the square root is defined only for non-negative arguments, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{7}+\\frac{(y+8)^{2}}{2}-1 & \\ge 0 \\\\ \\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{7}+\\frac{(y+8)^{2}}{2} & \\ge 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives the exterior of the ellipse $\\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{7}+\\frac{(y+8)^{2}}{2}=1,$ which includes the boundary.\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{7}+\\frac{(y+8)^{2}}{2}\\ge 1}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-74015" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bf97a5acc6acd2fe54bfdd2de22861374226df9798b45f6cf8422eff6e03593a"} {"question" "q-74015" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-74015" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{7}+\\frac{(y+8)^{2}}{2}\\ge 1}"] ["math" "{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{7}+\\frac{(y+8)^{2}}{2}\\le 1}"] ["math" "{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{7}+{y}^{2}\\le 1}"] ["math" "{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{7}+\\frac{(y+8)^{2}}{2}\\ge 1}"] ["text" "The entire $xy$-plane"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-74015" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{7}+\\frac{(y+8)^{2}}{2}\\ge 1}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-164232" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the hyperboloid of two sheets ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}=-1$, find the domain of $z=z(x,y).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-164232" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the hyperboloid equation, we make $z$ the subject as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-{z}^{2} & =-1 \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1 & ={z}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{2} & =1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} \\\\ {z}^{2} & =\\pm \\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe square root is defined only for non-negative arguments. However, notice that for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ge 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $z(x,y)$ is ${R}^{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-164232" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bf97a5acc6acd2fe54bfdd2de22861374226df9798b45f6cf8422eff6e03593a"} {"question" "q-164232" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-164232" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<1}"] ["math" "{(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>1}"] ["math" "{(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ge 1}"] ["math" "{(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 1}"] ["math" "{R}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-164232" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{R}^{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-164303" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the hyperboloid of two sheets $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{16}=-1,$ find the domain of $z=z(x,y).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-164303" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the hyperboloid equation, we make $z$ the subject as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{16} & =-1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}+1 & =\\frac{{z}^{2}}{16}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{z}^{2}}{16} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}+1 \\\\ {z}^{2} & =16(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}+1) \\\\ z & =\\pm 4\\sqrt{\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe square root is defined only for non-negative arguments. However, notice that for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}+1\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $z(x,y)$ is ${R}^{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-164303" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bf97a5acc6acd2fe54bfdd2de22861374226df9798b45f6cf8422eff6e03593a"} {"question" "q-164303" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-164303" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}<1}"] ["math" "{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}>1}"] ["math" "{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}\\ge 1}"] ["math" "{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}\\le 1}"] ["math" "{R}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-164303" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{R}^{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-164305" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the hyperboloid of two sheets ${x}^{2}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{9}-{z}^{2}=-1,$ find the domain of $z=z(x,y).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-164305" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the hyperboloid equation, we make $z$ the subject as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{9}-{z}^{2} & =-1 \\\\ {x}^{2}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{9}+1 & ={z}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{2} & ={x}^{2}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{9}+1 \\\\ z & =\\pm \\sqrt{{x}^{2}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{9}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe square root is defined only for non-negative arguments. However, notice that for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{9}+1\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $z(x,y)$ is ${R}^{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-164305" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bf97a5acc6acd2fe54bfdd2de22861374226df9798b45f6cf8422eff6e03593a"} {"question" "q-164305" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-164305" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{9}<1}"] ["math" "{(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{9}>1}"] ["math" "{(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{9}\\ge 1}"] ["math" "{(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{9}\\le 1}"] ["math" "{R}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-164305" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{R}^{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-164379" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The projection of the intersection between the hyperboloid of two sheets ${x}^{2}-\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{3}+\\frac{(z+3)^{2}}{12}=-1$ and the plane $x=\\sqrt{2}$ onto the $yz$-plane is a hyperbola. What are the lengths of the semi-axes of the hyperbola?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-164379" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the intersection of the hyperboloid and the plane $x=\\sqrt{2},$ we substitute $x=\\sqrt{2}$ into the equation of the hyperboloid:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\sqrt{2})^{2}-\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{3}+\\frac{(z+3)^{2}}{12} & =-1 \\\\ 2-\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{3}+\\frac{(z+3)^{2}}{12} & =-1 \\\\ -\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{3}+\\frac{(z+3)^{2}}{12} & =-3 \\\\ \\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{3}-\\frac{(z+3)^{2}}{12} & =3 \\\\ \\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{9}-\\frac{(z+3)^{2}}{36} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{{3}^{2}}-\\frac{(z+3)^{2}}{{6}^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of a hyperbola with semi-axes of lengths $3$ and $6.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-164379" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bf97a5acc6acd2fe54bfdd2de22861374226df9798b45f6cf8422eff6e03593a"} {"question" "q-164379" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-164379" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$3$ and $12$"] ["text" "$3$ and $6$"] ["text" "$9$ and $36$"] ["text" "$\\sqrt{3}$ and $2\\sqrt{3}$"] ["text" "$\\sqrt{3}$ and $\\sqrt{6}$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-164379" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$3$ and $6$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-35410" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The projection of the intersection between the hyperboloid of one sheet $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{18}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{50}=1$ and the plane $x=2$ onto the $yz$-plane is a hyperbola. What are the lengths of the semi-axes of the hyperbola?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-35410" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the intersection of the hyperboloid and the plane $x=2$, we substitute $x=2$ into the equation of the hyperboloid:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(2)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{18}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{50} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{18}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{50} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{18}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{50} & =1-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{18}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{50} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{25} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{{3}^{2}}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{{5}^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of a hyperbola with semi-axes of lengths $3$ and $5.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-35410" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bf97a5acc6acd2fe54bfdd2de22861374226df9798b45f6cf8422eff6e03593a"} {"question" "q-35410" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-35410" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$18$ and $50$"] ["text" "$3$ and $5$"] ["text" "$36$ and $100$"] ["text" "$3\\sqrt{2}$ and $5\\sqrt{2}$"] ["text" "$6\\sqrt{2}$ and $10\\sqrt{2}$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-35410" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$3$ and $5$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-71966" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the projection of the intersection between the hyperboloid of one sheet $\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{8}+{z}^{2}=1$ and the plane $z=1$ onto the $xy$-plane?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-71966" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the intersection of the hyperboloid and the plane $z=1$, we substitute $z=1$ into the equation of the hyperboloid:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{8}+{1}^{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{8}+1 & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{8} & =0 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4(x-2)^{2} \\\\ y & =\\pm 2(x-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us two intersecting lines: $y=2(x-2)$ and $y=-2(x-2).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-71966" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bf97a5acc6acd2fe54bfdd2de22861374226df9798b45f6cf8422eff6e03593a"} {"question" "q-71966" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-71966" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "A hyperbola: $\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{8}=-1$"] ["text" "A hyperbola: $\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{8}=1$"] ["text" "An ellipse: $\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{8}=1$"] ["text" "Two intersecting lines: $y=\\pm 2(x-2)$"] ["text" "Two parallel lines: $y=2x\\pm 2$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-71966" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "Two intersecting lines: $y=\\pm 2(x-2)$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-164380" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The projection of the intersection between the hyperboloid of two sheets $-\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{18}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}+(z-2)^{2}=-1$ and the plane $z=3$ onto the $xy$-plane is a hyperbola. What are the lengths of the semi-axes of the hyperbola?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-164380" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the intersection of the hyperboloid and the plane $z=3,$ we substitute $z=3$ into the equation of the hyperboloid:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{18}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}+(3-2)^{2} & =-1 \\\\ -\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{18}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}+1 & =-1 \\\\ -\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{18}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2} & =-2 \\\\ \\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{18}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2} & =2 \\\\ \\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{36}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{{6}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{2}^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of a hyperbola with semi-axes of lengths $6$ and $2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-164380" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bf97a5acc6acd2fe54bfdd2de22861374226df9798b45f6cf8422eff6e03593a"} {"question" "q-164380" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-164380" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$18$ and $2$"] ["text" "$3\\sqrt{2}$ and $\\sqrt{2}$"] ["text" "$6$ and $2$"] ["text" "$9$ and $4$"] ["text" "$\\sqrt{6}$ and $\\sqrt{3}$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-164380" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$6$ and $2$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-164377" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the trace in the $yz$-plane of the hyperboloid of two sheets ${x}^{2}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{3}=-1?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-164377" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the trace in the $yz$-plane, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the hyperboloid. This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{0}^{2}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{3} & =-1 \\\\ -\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{3} & =-1 \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{3} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is the equation of a hyperbola in $yz$-plane." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-164377" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bf97a5acc6acd2fe54bfdd2de22861374226df9798b45f6cf8422eff6e03593a"} {"question" "q-164377" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-164377" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{3}=1"] ["math" "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{3}=1"] ["math" "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}-{x}^{2}=1"] ["math" "\\frac{{z}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1"] ["math" "{x}^{2}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "q-164377" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{3}=1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ffeb665a1ed9fcffca0a115756eca7ec5a61cd5cef180d3dea24910b44382a8"} {"question" "e-12555" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the hyperboloid of one sheet  $\\dfrac{(x-3)^2}9 + \\dfrac{(y+4)^2}{16} - \\dfrac{(z-5)^2}{25} = 1,$ find its intercepts with the $x$-axis." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/example-12555.json" "file_sha256" "48d2ad29f324f3f469da6b4938530a5a0ce829565ac6fb77f85e644feace1e96"} {"question" "e-12555" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the $x$-intercepts, we plug $y=0$ and $z=0$ into the equation: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(0+4)^{2}}{16}-\\frac{(0-5)^{2}}{25} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{9}+1-1 & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ (x-3)^{2} & =9 \\\\ x-3 & =\\pm \\sqrt{9} \\\\ x & =3\\pm 3 \\\\ x & =0,6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $x$-axis are $(0,0,0)$ and $(6,0,0).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/example-12555.json" "file_sha256" "48d2ad29f324f3f469da6b4938530a5a0ce829565ac6fb77f85e644feace1e96"} {"question" "e-5265" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the hyperboloid of two sheets $(x-1)^2 + y^2 - \\dfrac{z^2}{4} = -1,$ find the domain of $z = z(x,y).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/example-5265.json" "file_sha256" "93419b7d0aefdc0b3264d829c9fe991641e899a5379b1334ab1e732d21f608b0"} {"question" "e-5265" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the hyperboloid equation, we make $z$ the subject as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-1)^{2}+{y}^{2}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4} & =-1 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+{y}^{2}+1 & =\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4} & =(x-1)^{2}+{y}^{2}+1 \\\\ {z}^{2} & =4((x-1)^{2}+{y}^{2}+1) \\\\ z & =\\pm 2\\sqrt{(x-1)^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe square root is defined only for non-negative arguments. However, notice that for all $(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2,$ we have\n\n$$\n(x-1)^2 + y^2 + 1 \\geq 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $z(x,y)$ is $\\mathbb R^2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/example-5265.json" "file_sha256" "93419b7d0aefdc0b3264d829c9fe991641e899a5379b1334ab1e732d21f608b0"} {"question" "e-6078" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The projection of the intersection between the hyperboloid of two sheets \n\n$$\n-\\dfrac{(x-5)^2}{8} + \\dfrac{y^2}{50} + (z-3)^2 = -1\n$$\n\nand the plane $z = 4$ onto the $xy$-plane is a hyperbola. What are the lengths of the semi-axes of the hyperbola?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/example-6078.json" "file_sha256" "e12291c210815da56102a28c01d313e31eb04a1c5a338502ce1b9e6d64f3e532"} {"question" "e-6078" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the intersection of the hyperboloid and the plane $z = 4,$ we substitute $z = 4$ into the equation of the hyperboloid:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{50}+(z-3)^{2} & =-1 \\\\ -\\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{50}+1=-1 \\\\ -\\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{50} & =-2 \\\\ \\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{8}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{50} & =2 \\\\ \\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{16}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{100} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{{4}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{10}^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of a hyperbola with semi-axes of lengths $4$ and $10.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042406/example-6078.json" "file_sha256" "e12291c210815da56102a28c01d313e31eb04a1c5a338502ce1b9e6d64f3e532"}] "usage" {"e-6078" [] "e-5265" [] "q-164232" [] "q-164380" [] "q-35410" [] "e-12555" []} "basis" 1548 "retractions" [[17592186124743 :question/problem "Given the hyperboloid of two sheets $x^{2} + y^{2} - z^{2} =-1$, find the domain of $z = z(x, y)$."] [17592186124798 :question/problem "The projection of the intersection between the hyperboloid of one sheet $\\frac{x^{2}}{8} + ((y - 4)^{2})/(18) - \\frac{z^{2}}{50} = 1$ and the plane $x = 2$ onto the $yz$-plane is a hyperbola. What are the lengths of the semi-axes of the hyperbola?"] [17592186124131 :question/problem "Given the hyperboloid of one sheet $\\dfrac{(x-3)^2}9 + \\dfrac{(y+4)^2}{16} - \\dfrac{(z-5)^2}{25} = 1$, find its intercepts with the $x$-axis."] [17592186124131 :question/worked-solution "To find the $x$-intercepts, we plug $y=0$ and $z=0$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n((x - 3)^{2})/(9) + ((0 + 4)^{2})/(16) - ((0 - 5)^{2})/(25) &= 1 \\\\\n((x - 3)^{2})/(9) + 1 - 1 &= 1 \\\\\n((x - 3)^{2})/(9) &= 1 \\\\\n(x - 3)^{2} &= 9 \\\\\nx - 3 &= ± \\sqrt{9} \\\\\nx &= 3 ± 3 \\\\\nx &= 0, 6\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $x$-axis are $(0,0,0)$ and $(6,0,0)$."] [17592186124227 :question/problem "Given the hyperboloid of two sheets $(x-1)^2 + y^2 - \\dfrac{z^2}{4} = -1$, find the domain of $z = z(x,y)$."] [17592186124227 :question/worked-solution "From the hyperboloid equation, we make $z$ the subject as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(x - 1)^{2} + y^{2} - \\frac{z^{2}}{4} &= -1 \\\\\n(x - 1)^{2} + y^{2} + 1 &= \\frac{z^{2}}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{z^{2}}{4} &= (x - 1)^{2} + y^{2} + 1 \\\\\nz^{2} &= 4((x - 1)^{2} + y^{2} + 1) \\\\\nz &= ± 2\\sqrt{(x - 1)^{2} + y^{2} + 1}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe square root is defined only for non-negative arguments. However, notice that for all $(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2$, we have\n\n$$\n(x-1)^2 + y^2 + 1 \\geq 0\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $z(x,y)$ is $\\mathbb R^2$."] [17592186124282 :question/problem "The projection of the intersection between the hyperboloid of two sheets\n$-\\dfrac{(x-5)^2}{8} + \\dfrac{y^2}{50} + (z-3)^2 = -1$\nand the plane $z = 4$ onto the $xy$-plane is a hyperbola. What are the lengths of the semi-axes of the hyperbola?"] [17592186124282 :question/worked-solution "To find the intersection of the hyperboloid and the plane $z = 4$, we substitute $z = 4$ into the equation of the hyperboloid:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n- ((x - 5)^{2})/(8) + \\frac{y^{2}}{50} + (z - 3)^{2} &= -1 \\\\\n&= - ((x - 5)^{2})/(8) + \\frac{y^{2}}{50} + 1 =-1 \\\\\n- ((x - 5)^{2})/(8) + \\frac{y^{2}}{50} &= -2 \\\\\n((x - 5)^{2})/(8) - \\frac{y^{2}}{50} &= 2 \\\\\n((x - 5)^{2})/(16) - \\frac{y^{2}}{100} &= 1 \\\\\n((x - 5)^{2})/(4^{2}) - \\frac{y^{2}}{10^{2}} &= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of a hyperbola with semi-axes of lengths $4$ and $10$."]] "immutable_answers" [17592186121478 17592186121479 17592186121480 17592186121481 17592186121482 17592186121811 17592186121812 17592186121813 17592186121814 17592186121815 17592186294589 17592186294590 17592186294591 17592186294592 17592186294593] "immutable_fields" [[17592186121477 :answer-field/correct] [17592186121477 :answer-field/id] [17592186121477 :answer-field/key] [17592186121477 :answer-field/type] [17592186121810 :answer-field/correct] [17592186121810 :answer-field/id] [17592186121810 :answer-field/key] [17592186121810 :answer-field/type] [17592186294588 :answer-field/correct] [17592186294588 :answer-field/id] [17592186294588 :answer-field/key] [17592186294588 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
